      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T20:52:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My guess with why we were seeing increased performance with a larger SSBO block size is that it avoids thrashing re-binding the SSBOs. \n\nWith the original tracker, we\u0027d always ask for an SSBO that held all of the data for a given pipeline (N*`uniformDataSize`) so if that was bigger than the default block size, we\u0027d still get a single SSBO.  Now, we would spread out the data into several buffers and then depending on the sorting arrangement end up with more rebinds.\n\nWe could experiment with adding the extra check for `|| (usesStorageBuffers \u0026\u0026 uniformData.fGpuData.fBuffer !\u003d fLastBinding.fBuffer)` to the if. This would have the behavior of duplicating the data into the current buffer to avoid introducing a rebind.\n\nI\u0027m not sure whether or not that buys us anything, or if the increased SSBO size default isn\u0027t that significant, and would then be entirely mitigated by the adaptive buffer sizing across frames. The adaptive buffer sizing would still work with the redundant upload approach although we would be causing the BufferManager to think it needed more space than it really did (which should then trend towards 0 overestimate with subsequent frames using bigger starting buffers).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 192,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 192,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "35b47140be87610663b004b40ab539aeec16f541",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9498ebf_6d1d36c0",
