        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T20:52:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can (if it gives us any performance boost), use a single `UniformDataCache2` here now since the paint uniforms now have the same cache lifetime as the step uniforms.\n\nThe requirement is that now `UniformDataCache2::Index` has to be able to hold `2*DrawList::kMaxRenderSteps+1` (and with an adjusted `kInvalidIndex` value), to be able to handle the case where each renderstep draw has both a unique paint uniform and a unique step uniform value.\n\nRight now with the restricted `kMaxRenderStep` count the SortKey already satisfies this, and hopefully we can get down to storing a single binding index in follow up work and then the bit count requirement goes back to just `kMaxRenderSteps` because the indices would be assigned to the tuple of uniform values in aggregate.",
